LLOOAADDEERR TTUUNNAABBLLEE
     The following tunable can be set at the loader(8) prompt before booting
     the kernel, or stored in loader.conf(5).

     _h_w_._u_s_b_._q_u_i_r_k_._%_d
             The value is a string whose format is:

                   "VendorId ProductId LowRevision HighRevision UQ_QUIRK,..."

             Installs the quirks UUQQ__QQUUIIRRKK,,...... for all USB devices matching
             VVeennddoorrIIdd and PPrroodduuccttIIdd which have a hardware revision between and
             including LLoowwRReevviissiioonn and HHiigghhRReevviissiioonn.

             VVeennddoorrIIdd, PPrroodduuccttIIdd, LLoowwRReevviissiioonn and HHiigghhRReevviissiioonn are all 16 bits
             numbers which can be decimal or hexadecimal based.

             A maximum of 100 variables hhww..uussbb..qquuiirrkk..00,, ..11,, ......,, ..9999 can be
             defined.

             If a matching entry is found in the kernel's internal quirks ta‐
             ble, it is replaced by the new definition.

             Else a new entry is created given that the quirk table is not
             full.

             The kernel iterates over the hhww..uussbb..qquuiirrkk..NN variables starting at
             NN == 00 and stops at NN == 9999 or the first non-existing one.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     After attaching a uu33gg device which appears as a USB device on _u_g_e_n_0_._3:

           usbconfig -d ugen0.3 add_quirk UQ_MSC_EJECT_WAIT

     Enable a Holtec/Keep Out F85 gaming keyboard on _u_g_e_n_1_._4:

           usbconfig -d ugen1.4 add_quirk UQ_KBD_BOOTPROTO

     To install a quirk at boot time, place one or several lines like the fol‐
     lowing in loader.conf(5):

           hw.usb.quirk.0="0x04d9 0xfa50 0 0xffff UQ_KBD_IGNORE"

